From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: scan video device nodes up to /dev/video63

getDeviceInfosForType() only opens /dev/video0 to /dev/video9. With
camss enabled on SC8280XP, camss alone registers 32 video nodes and the
codec nodes come after them (video32 and video33 on the Huawei MateBook
E Go). No device is found for the decoders and encoders, and every
codec falls back to software while the component names still appear in
MediaCodecList. The numbering depends on probe order, so the codec
nodes cannot be pinned to low numbers.

Scan up to /dev/video63. The extra open() calls fail at once, and only
on the first call, since the result is cached in sDeviceInfosCache.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp b/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
index f8df182..d72219a 100644
--- a/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
@@ -2564,7 +2564,10 @@ const V4L2Device::DeviceInfos& V4L2Device::getDeviceInfosForType(V4L2Device::Typ
     }
 
     DeviceInfos deviceInfos;
-    for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
+    // Camera drivers can register many video nodes before the codec (camss alone
+    // registers 32), and the numbering depends on probe order, so scan a wider range.
+    static constexpr int kMaxVideoDeviceIndex = 64;
+    for (int i = 0; i < kMaxVideoDeviceIndex; ++i) {
         std::string path = base::StringPrintf("%s%d", kVideoDevicePattern, i);
 
         scoped_refptr<V4L2Device> device = V4L2Device::create();
